    given-names: K.
    alias: chenhk1113-HK
    affiliation: chenhk1113-HK/sidm-composite-dm-mediator
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/chenhk1113-HK/sidm-composite-dm-mediator
keywords:
  - dark-matter
  - sidm
  - self-interacting-dark-matter
  - secluded-wimp
  - composite-dark-matter
  - dark-glueball
  - dark-rho
  - dark-baryon
  - mediator-detection
  - bayesian-inference
  - dynesty
  - gravothermal-collapse
  - direct-detection
  - lz
  - fermi-lat
  - dwarf-galaxies
abstract: >
  Bayesian constraint pipeline for self-interacting dark matter (SIDM)
  cross-sections, with a composite-DM microphysics extension (dark
  glueballs, dark rho, dark baryons) and a secluded-mediator detection
  feasibility survey. Headline result: sigma/m ~ 1-3 cm^2/g at galactic
  velocity scales (1.4-1.7 cm^2/g MAP), velocity index a ~ 0.6-1.4, with
  the mediator invisible to all direct-detection experiments (sigma_SI ~
  2e-118 cm^2, ~10^46 times below the LZ WS2024 neutrino floor and ~10^50
  times below LZ SR1+SR3). Cross-validated against Drobczyk 2025
  (arXiv:2506.22997). See docs/MATHEMATICS.md, docs/DATA_SOURCES.md, and
  the per-version synthesis docs in v0.3-prelim/docs/ for full derivation.
